{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:02G1:proof", "parent_tag": "01V4", "chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "risk_level": "R3", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "The statement is local on <MATH_0001> and <MATH_0002>.\nBy Lemma <REF_0001>\nabove we may assume that <MATH_0003> is a standard smooth morphism of affines.\nIn this case the result follows from\nAlgebra, Lemma <REF_0002>\n(and the definition of a relative global complete intersection, see\nAlgebra,\nDefinition <REF_0003>).\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-smooth-locally-standard-smooth}", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "REF_0002": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-standard-smooth}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{algebra-definition-relative-global-complete-intersection}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:9eab51c6481ea821abf329e4b95f32146fb8bb6278faacffcf2a2a48be08e2a7", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:96c3411e6a9a1162186a01b59fe58a9bbc8931d4a803ccd33bc7f22be35ca722", "source_math_hash": "sha256:beeb8661638c47d765a00dd03e05eaf667d19386bda70e80fdb479caff003264"}
{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:01V4:prose-0005", "parent_tag": "01V4", "chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "risk_level": "R2", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLemma <REF_0001>\nsays that the following definition makes sense.\n\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-smooth-omega-finite-locally-free}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:001b3d129f9e3d5c7bc90028a69db293c1c9efd3b97c02ef7f864146f56c383a", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3a5aa1c1d6e342350538952d0e5c35066cd3e963f5408195a1645de4a415a825", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a"}
{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:02G2:statement", "parent_tag": "01V4", "chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "definition", "risk_level": "R3", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an integer. We say a morphism of schemes <MATH_0002>\nis <TEXTITOPEN_0001>smooth of relative dimension <MATH_0003><TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if <MATH_0004> is smooth and\n<MATH_0005> is finite locally free of constant rank <MATH_0006>.\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$d \\geq 0$", "MATH_0002": "$f : X \\to S$", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "MATH_0003": "$d$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "MATH_0004": "$f$", "MATH_0005": "$\\Omega_{X/S}$", "MATH_0006": "$d$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-smooth-relative-dimension}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:b2d299c162c7cc7cc15d3be986b22c8f85ef9ac4369f469d47aa56eeb4fc9a0e", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:54bc128de6a66e85060d6e6f118c064e4ebeae1d27d6c748c07b936daa796df3", "source_math_hash": "sha256:519143f72ed370f86f046f522016556e7d4c60f04772407e54312f7b02fdb71d"}
{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:01V4:prose-0006", "parent_tag": "01V4", "chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "risk_level": "R2", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn other words, <MATH_0001> is smooth and the nonempty fibres are equidimensional\nof dimension <MATH_0002>. By Lemma <REF_0001> below this is also\nthe same as requiring: (a) <MATH_0003> is locally of finite presentation, (b) <MATH_0004> is\nflat, (c) all nonempty fibres equidimensional of dimension <MATH_0005>, and (d)\n<MATH_0006> finite locally free of rank <MATH_0007>. It is not enough to simply\nassume that <MATH_0008> is flat, of finite presentation, and <MATH_0009> is\nfinite locally free of rank <MATH_0010>. A counter example is given by\n<MATH_0011>.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nHere is a differential criterion of smoothness at a point.\nThere are many variants of this result\nall of which may be useful at some point. We will just add them\nhere as needed.\n\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "MATH_0001": "$f$", "MATH_0002": "$d$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-smooth-at-point}", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "MATH_0004": "$f$", "MATH_0005": "$d$", "MATH_0006": "$\\Omega_{X/S}$", "MATH_0007": "$d$", "MATH_0008": "$f$", "MATH_0009": "$\\Omega_{X/S}$", "MATH_0010": "$d$", "MATH_0011": "$\\Spec(\\mathbf{F}_p[t]) \\to \\Spec(\\mathbf{F}_p[t^p])$", "STRUCT_0002": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0003": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:09d130e6d08ec4529692bc0e640357c5466a209b7a4e397341a446f115eb5870", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:222929178f51ba57e31def993ce8dccf1dcc4ce9d888a67004c33f096a7d5dfb", "source_math_hash": "sha256:87ea0541ccab50e2910b872f276bb06d0b68d7b669c799a8e3ed7598ad3a70d8"}
